# Project rules (always apply)

Canonical sources (read before product changes):

1. `docs/ai-development-rules.md`
2. `docs/governance/` (`MANIFEST.json`; `npm run verify:governance:docs`)
3. `docs/project-intelligence-summary.md`
4. `docs/scroll-architecture-rules.md`
5. `docs/governance/runtime-workspace-scroll-authority.md`
6. `docs/mobile-testing-rules.md`
7. `docs/deployment-rules.md`
8. `docs/ui-ux-rules.md`
9. `docs/performance-rules.md`

Repo-root `.cursorrules` is the session summary. Do not invent parallel policy.

## Session discipline

- Acknowledge architecture + scroll + mobile + deployment constraints before writing product code.
- No feature complete without mobile validation when UI/layout/sticky/overlays/responsive behavior changed.
- No shipped user-facing work without `npm run build`, `npm run qa:governance` (from `lender-app/`), `npm run deploy:prod`, and production smoke — unless exempt per `docs/deployment-rules.md`.

## Commands (`cwd: lender-app/`)

- `npm run qa:governance` — automated pre-complete gate
- `npm run verify:governance:docs` — required policy files exist
- `npm run deploy:prod` — build + Vercel production deploy (CLI)
